WEBVTT

00:15.813 --> 00:17.775
(MUFFLED RUMBLING)

00:22.248 --> 00:24.452
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:32.026 --> 00:32.996
(DOOR CLOSES)

00:33.098 --> 00:35.566
(MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS)

00:35.668 --> 00:37.266
How can I help you?

00:37.368 --> 00:38.831
(IN BRITISH ACCENT) Uh,
can I get a black coffee?

00:38.933 --> 00:40.600
Sure.

00:46.711 --> 00:47.679
Thank you.

00:47.781 --> 00:49.273
(INDISTINCT CHATTER, LAUGHTER)

00:49.375 --> 00:51.545
(INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING)

00:56.248 --> 00:57.782
(MUSIC STOPS)

00:58.991 --> 01:00.224
-(CHAIR SLIDES)
-(MUSIC RESUMES)

01:05.396 --> 01:08.163
-(MUSIC, CHATTER QUIETENS)
-(MUFFLED BUZZING)

01:08.265 --> 01:10.432
(INDISTINCT CHATTER,
LAUGHTER RESUMES)

01:13.006 --> 01:15.173
-(CHATTER QUIETENS)
-(MUFFLED BUZZING)

01:15.906 --> 01:18.110
(CHATTER RESUMES)

01:18.979 --> 01:21.146
(INTRIGUING MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

01:26.115 --> 01:27.284
(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS)

01:38.592 --> 01:40.759
(INTRIGUING MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

01:50.302 --> 01:51.473
(CHAIR SLIDES)

01:52.108 --> 01:53.739
(FAINT, MUFFLED BUZZING)

01:54.274 --> 01:55.980
(CLEARS THROAT)

01:56.082 --> 01:58.046
I love that book so much.
It's, uh...

01:58.148 --> 01:59.246
I just finished it last week.

01:59.348 --> 02:01.248
It's incredible.
It's... (STUTTERS)

02:01.350 --> 02:04.486
I really, really,
really admire it.

02:04.921 --> 02:05.820
And, uh...

02:05.922 --> 02:07.225
(CUP CLANGING)

02:08.929 --> 02:10.024
-(DOOR OPENS)
-(LOUD CHATTER)

02:10.126 --> 02:11.493
(CLEARS THROAT) Uh...

02:12.692 --> 02:14.963
(SOFTLY) All right.
(CLEARS THROAT)

02:15.065 --> 02:17.268
(INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING)

02:23.507 --> 02:25.469
(STUTTERING)
Um, I'm sorry. I didn't mean...

02:25.572 --> 02:28.513
(ROMANTIC '80s POP MUSIC
PLAYING)

02:28.615 --> 02:30.474
(MUFFLED SPEECH)

02:30.577 --> 02:32.017
CHARLIE: I wasn't... Genuinely,

02:32.119 --> 02:33.180
-I really admire the book.
-What? Sorry?

02:33.282 --> 02:34.786
I was just saying, I'm not...

02:34.888 --> 02:36.655
I'm not hitting on you. I...

02:36.757 --> 02:37.682
Sorry, what do you mean?

02:37.784 --> 02:39.552
Genuinely,
I just really admire the book.

02:39.654 --> 02:41.891
(INDISTINCT CHATTER
CONTINUES IN BACKGROUND)

02:41.993 --> 02:42.989
I'm deaf in this one.

02:43.091 --> 02:44.092
You're deaf?

02:44.195 --> 02:46.730
Yeah. This one though. I can...

02:46.832 --> 02:49.263
(LAUGHS AWKWARDLY)

02:49.365 --> 02:51.632
-(EMMA CHUCKLES SOFTLY)
-Uh...

02:54.874 --> 02:57.309
Yeah, the, uh... (SIGHS)

02:57.811 --> 02:58.771
Do you want to start over?

03:00.608 --> 03:03.012
-Um...
-We could just try it again?

03:03.114 --> 03:04.412
-Maybe?
-You wanna try...

03:04.514 --> 03:06.350
-Just do it again?
-EMMA: Yeah. Do it again.

03:08.516 --> 03:09.881
-Okay.
-Okay. (CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

03:19.030 --> 03:21.065
(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)

03:21.167 --> 03:23.361
CHARLIE:
 "I was absolutely certain

03:23.463 --> 03:25.034
 "I was being trapped

03:25.136 --> 03:26.567
"and that you were recording me

03:26.669 --> 03:29.170
 "and I was gonna be
 all over the Internet,

03:29.272 --> 03:30.769
 "but I now understand..."

03:30.871 --> 03:33.306
"...that the only thing
that could have saved me

03:33.408 --> 03:34.878
"was a second first impression."

03:34.980 --> 03:36.575
Yeah. So funny. Great.

03:36.677 --> 03:38.280
So I'm gonna start there
and then go on

03:38.382 --> 03:39.677
 -to the first date.
-MIKE: Good.

03:39.779 --> 03:41.718
EMMA: So what'd you think
of the ending?

03:41.820 --> 03:42.713
Ending? Of what?

03:42.815 --> 03:44.248
EMMA: Of the book.
I just finished it.

03:44.350 --> 03:45.653
Oh, the, um...

03:45.755 --> 03:48.926
I don't know. I feel like
I didn't get it, you know.

03:49.028 --> 03:51.261
Like I was missing something.

03:51.363 --> 03:52.658
Yeah, no, I know what you mean.
I think...

03:52.761 --> 03:54.364
Yeah, me neither, really.
(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

03:54.466 --> 03:56.727
'Cause did she die?
Is that... (CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

03:56.829 --> 03:58.501
Like, do you think
that's what it was?

03:59.466 --> 04:01.339
I think so. I think so.

04:02.307 --> 04:03.737
Just, that doesn't make
any sense.

04:04.337 --> 04:05.707
It doesn't?

04:05.809 --> 04:07.572
Well, no, 'cause you remember
this, like, the mirror thing?

04:07.674 --> 04:09.644
CHARLIE: Hm.
Wait, which mirror?

04:10.679 --> 04:13.377
The whole thing at the end
with the mirror.

04:13.479 --> 04:15.849
Um... (SMACKS LIPS)

04:15.951 --> 04:19.920
I thought it was just more of
a kind of metaphor for like...

04:20.022 --> 04:21.557
Uh...

04:21.659 --> 04:24.389
I just didn't really realize
it was real in the sense

04:24.491 --> 04:27.325
that the mirror was, um...

04:27.427 --> 04:28.867
The mirror was...

04:28.969 --> 04:30.365
(SIGHS) I don't even know...

04:30.467 --> 04:31.498
I don't even know
where to take this.

04:31.600 --> 04:33.938
I didn't read the book.
And, um... yeah.

04:34.041 --> 04:35.566
-What?
-I think I just glitched

04:35.668 --> 04:37.603
when I saw you... (STUTTERS)

04:37.705 --> 04:39.473
...and I just wanted
to talk to you.

04:39.575 --> 04:42.710
And I didn't have anything,
so...

04:43.750 --> 04:44.745
That's weird.

04:48.948 --> 04:50.856
Um, yeah, I'm...
Well, I'm sorry. I didn't...

04:50.958 --> 04:52.786
Just a weird, little freak.

04:53.620 --> 04:55.288
Weird, little British freak.

04:55.390 --> 04:56.658
-Oh, yeah?
-(CHUCKLES)

04:56.760 --> 04:58.963
I'm sorry. I didn't realize
you actually doubled down.

04:59.065 --> 05:00.462
Yeah, what was I supposed to do?

05:00.564 --> 05:02.434
-How about reading the book?
-(CHARLIE SIGHS)

05:02.536 --> 05:05.297
For a first date? I don't know.
That's a lot weirder, no?

05:05.399 --> 05:07.403
How is that weirder?

05:07.506 --> 05:10.073
I don't know.
It just feels weirder somehow.

05:10.175 --> 05:12.005
Okay. Don't agree, but go on.

05:12.108 --> 05:13.145
(CHUCKLES)

05:13.247 --> 05:16.807
So, I wanna say this thing
about her laugh.

05:16.909 --> 05:18.415
Do you know
how it's kind of like...

05:18.517 --> 05:20.949
It's very cute,
but it's also kind of like...

05:21.051 --> 05:24.122
(CHORTLING)

05:24.224 --> 05:25.984
-Repulsive even. Okay.
-CHARLIE: Yeah.

05:26.086 --> 05:29.194
And then if, uh, she laughs,
then I can point it out

05:29.296 --> 05:30.594
and be like,
"And there it is!" you know.

05:30.696 --> 05:32.295
I did. I said, "If everyone
knows he's a piece of shit,

05:32.397 --> 05:33.832
"then why are we doing
a retrospective

05:33.934 --> 05:34.793
"in the first place?"

05:34.896 --> 05:36.695
It's like, it's so incredibly
irresponsible.

05:36.797 --> 05:38.468
No one ever cares
until it's too late.

05:38.570 --> 05:40.504
And then it always ends up
backfiring on me...

05:44.277 --> 05:45.904
Emma, I'm being serious.
It's not funny.

05:46.006 --> 05:48.809
No, I agree with you.
This is not funny at all.

05:49.982 --> 05:51.449
It's very serious.

05:53.820 --> 05:54.950
(SNICKERS)

05:55.052 --> 05:55.913
You're laughing.

05:56.016 --> 05:57.815
CHARLIE: "I love how you
 always find a way

05:57.917 --> 06:00.858
 "to turn my drama
 into a comedy."

06:00.960 --> 06:02.256
And then, uh...

06:02.358 --> 06:03.722
-I don't know.
-What?

06:03.824 --> 06:05.924
I kind of wanna
say something about...

06:06.026 --> 06:09.096
-(MOANING IN PLEASURE)
-(RATTLING, CLATTERING)

06:09.198 --> 06:10.535
-No.
-No?

06:10.637 --> 06:12.737
Why do you want to talk about
fucking in front of your family?

06:12.839 --> 06:13.634
Or her family?

06:13.736 --> 06:14.998
No, I don't wanna
say it, like, directly.

06:15.100 --> 06:17.376
I just wanna kind of allude
to it somehow

06:17.478 --> 06:21.511
'cause I just think
we've always had this sort of...

06:21.613 --> 06:24.343
Like an incredible chemistry
that's just... I...

06:24.445 --> 06:25.717
Yeah, no, do that.

06:25.819 --> 06:27.315
Do exactly that.

06:27.418 --> 06:29.751
-Okay?
-Okay, what if I said...

06:30.318 --> 06:31.382
licentious.

06:31.484 --> 06:34.025
Or languorous.

06:34.128 --> 06:35.019
Just skip this part completely.

06:35.121 --> 06:37.025
What, and just go straight
to the crying thing?

06:37.127 --> 06:39.728
(EMMA SOBBING)

06:40.933 --> 06:42.401
(SHUDDERS)

06:43.000 --> 06:43.996
(SIGHS)

06:44.630 --> 06:45.632
It's just, you know,

06:45.734 --> 06:46.965
it's my first time
saying it out loud,

06:47.067 --> 06:49.406
so I feel like I'll get it
on the day, you know.

06:49.509 --> 06:51.309
Maybe you should start
with something funny,

06:51.411 --> 06:53.608
so you're not, like,
immediately in tears.

06:53.710 --> 06:56.509
But it's kind of sweet.
It's endearing.

06:56.611 --> 06:57.908
Yeah, but you wanna look good.

06:58.010 --> 06:59.215
Crying makes you look
kind of ugly.

06:59.318 --> 07:01.713
-What?
-You, the general you.

07:01.815 --> 07:02.946
-Like, women.
-(SIGHS SOFTLY)

07:03.048 --> 07:05.421
Um, what about
the first time you met?

07:05.523 --> 07:07.289
Wasn't that
kind of a funny story?

07:07.391 --> 07:09.093
I love that book. I just...

07:09.195 --> 07:11.289
Oh, no, she can't tell that one.

07:11.391 --> 07:12.393
Why not?

07:12.495 --> 07:14.065
What stories are you gonna do?

07:14.167 --> 07:15.194
What do you mean? For my speech?

07:15.296 --> 07:16.399
Yeah.

07:16.501 --> 07:18.368
Well, you'll just
have to wait and see.

07:18.470 --> 07:20.103
No, no, no.
So we don't, you know,

07:20.205 --> 07:22.933
like, say the same things.

07:23.035 --> 07:24.608
Are you gonna use
the first time we met?

07:25.140 --> 07:26.277
Yes.

07:26.379 --> 07:27.605
Okay, well,
what about the first date?

07:27.707 --> 07:29.710
-Yeah, of course.
-Fuck!

07:29.812 --> 07:32.246
(CHUCKLES)
You don't have to do a speech.

07:32.348 --> 07:34.211
(SIGHS) First kiss?

07:34.313 --> 07:36.815
EMMA: Wait, so you can just,
like, go in whenever?

07:36.917 --> 07:37.982
CHARLIE: Yeah,
I do it all the time.

07:38.084 --> 07:39.418
EMMA: Oh, so you bring
all the girls here?

07:39.520 --> 07:40.917
CHARLIE: Um, yeah.

07:41.019 --> 07:42.753
-(EMMA SCOFFS, LAUGHS) Ouch.
-No,

07:42.855 --> 07:44.054
when I'm working late and stuff.

07:44.156 --> 07:45.589
Yeah, when you're working late
and stuff.

07:45.691 --> 07:47.361
-Yeah.
-(SIGHS)

07:47.463 --> 07:48.564
Okay, this is like...

07:48.666 --> 07:49.930
This is like a childhood dream,
you know,

07:50.032 --> 07:54.506
like sneaking into a mall
or a library at night. It's...

07:56.509 --> 07:58.670
Well, your dreams
are about to come true.

07:58.773 --> 08:00.611
-Wow.
-(BOTH CHUCKLE SOFTLY)

08:03.083 --> 08:04.648
-(RATTLING)
-Um...

08:05.711 --> 08:06.882
Is it not working?

08:06.984 --> 08:08.148
Hm.

08:08.250 --> 08:09.246
(BEEPING)

08:12.189 --> 08:14.158
(RATTLING)

08:14.260 --> 08:16.660
-(ALARM BLARING)
-Oh, sh...

08:17.425 --> 08:19.531
Um... Ooh!

08:23.629 --> 08:25.935
(DOORS THUDDING)

08:26.038 --> 08:27.968
(GRUNTING)

08:32.112 --> 08:34.311
(ALARM GROWS MUFFLED)

08:34.413 --> 08:37.846
(MUFFLED ALARM
CONTINUES BLARING)

08:40.384 --> 08:42.518
Wait, so he trapped you?

08:42.620 --> 08:45.115
It wasn't planned, Rachel.
(CHUCKLES)

08:45.217 --> 08:46.887
What about that time
you thought you had a...

08:46.989 --> 08:48.520
-(CONTINUES INDISTINCTLY)
-(MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING)

08:48.622 --> 08:50.192
(MACHINERY WHIRRING)

08:50.294 --> 08:52.630
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

09:02.803 --> 09:04.475
-ALICE: Who was that?
-Hm?

09:04.577 --> 09:07.605
Oh, uh, it's just Charlie.
I left my wallet.

09:07.707 --> 09:09.074
Hm. Who's Charlie?

09:09.176 --> 09:12.611
Uh, he's my boyfriend, I guess.
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

09:12.713 --> 09:14.247
(INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING)

09:14.350 --> 09:15.917
(CHUCKLES)

09:17.419 --> 09:18.752
Are you okay?

09:18.854 --> 09:21.054
Yeah. No, I'm fine.
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

09:24.263 --> 09:26.092
(EMMA BREATHING HEAVILY)

09:28.562 --> 09:30.434
(INHALES DEEPLY)

09:30.536 --> 09:31.664
ALICE: I don't know.
 Can you just...

09:31.767 --> 09:33.204
 She's saying it's her chest...

09:33.306 --> 09:34.698
It's her heart. Her heart is...

09:34.800 --> 09:36.339
So what was it?

09:36.441 --> 09:38.905
It was just, like, feelings.

09:39.007 --> 09:41.376
-Feelings? What do you mean?
-EMMA: Yeah.

09:41.478 --> 09:42.544
Like intense butterflies.

09:42.646 --> 09:43.610
-Right?
-RACHEL: No, I get that,

09:43.712 --> 09:46.016
but it wasn't your first time.

09:46.118 --> 09:47.385
I don't know.

09:47.487 --> 09:50.086
So you're saying
Charlie is your first...

09:50.188 --> 09:51.818
Love... Yeah.

09:51.920 --> 09:54.318
Your first love
or your first crush?

09:56.557 --> 09:57.761
Both, I think.

09:58.629 --> 10:00.465
-What, is that insane?
-At 30?

10:00.567 --> 10:03.165
Well, I mean,
I was 28 when we met, so...

10:03.267 --> 10:04.229
RACHEL: Still!

10:05.470 --> 10:07.466
I don't know. I used to be ugly.

10:07.568 --> 10:09.003
Oh, come on!

10:09.735 --> 10:11.142
Don't freak out,

10:11.244 --> 10:12.810
but there's a giant spider

10:12.912 --> 10:15.607
that's crawling up your back
and it's almost into your hair.

10:15.709 --> 10:17.044
Just don't panic.

10:20.547 --> 10:21.480
Nothing?

10:21.582 --> 10:22.850
-No.
-No.

10:22.952 --> 10:24.948
I feel like
you just have to do it louder.

10:25.050 --> 10:26.955
(MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING FAINTLY)

10:29.161 --> 10:31.122
Okay. Um...

10:31.224 --> 10:33.830
(WHISPERING)
I love you so much it hurts.

10:34.795 --> 10:36.294
I can't be without you.

10:37.636 --> 10:39.633
It's scary
'cause I can't imagine...

10:39.735 --> 10:45.602
(CHARLIE CONTINUES, MUFFLED)

10:45.704 --> 10:49.241
(WHISPERING) I want to marry you
but I'm too afraid to even ask.

10:52.780 --> 10:54.114
I think I caught that.

10:55.582 --> 10:56.754
You did?

10:57.585 --> 10:58.756
A hairy knife?

10:59.223 --> 11:00.219
A what?

11:00.321 --> 11:02.155
Did you say something
about, like, a hairy knife?

11:03.393 --> 11:04.927
-No.
-No?

11:05.926 --> 11:07.097
Emma, that's not even a thing.

11:07.199 --> 11:08.667
(BOTH LAUGH)

11:09.399 --> 11:10.361
(SNIFFLES)

11:11.037 --> 11:12.268
You okay?

11:12.370 --> 11:14.805
Yeah. No, it's good.

11:14.907 --> 11:16.867
Oh, come on, you gotta be
a bit more specific than that.

11:16.969 --> 11:18.071
Yeah, it's a little corny

11:18.173 --> 11:20.642
in a wedding speech kind of way,
but it's, um...

11:20.744 --> 11:23.147
All the pieces are there,
you know.

11:23.249 --> 11:23.909
I think you have it.

11:24.011 --> 11:25.447
-(SNIFFLES)
-(CHARLIE WHEEZES)

11:25.549 --> 11:26.714
All right, you can't cry

11:26.816 --> 11:28.317
-and say it sucks.
-(MIKE LAUGHS)

11:28.419 --> 11:29.786
(SPEAKER CRACKLING)

11:29.888 --> 11:32.053
 (I WANT TO LAY WITH YOU
BY SHIRA SMALLS PLAYING)

11:33.887 --> 11:35.760
And looking at each other.

11:44.865 --> 11:47.068
(CHARLIE AND EMMA GIGGLE)

11:48.734 --> 11:49.906
Nice.

11:55.347 --> 11:58.145
Slide... and two.

12:03.254 --> 12:04.217
Nice.

12:07.853 --> 12:10.322
And kiss. Great.

12:12.892 --> 12:14.692
Ready and drag.

12:14.794 --> 12:16.064
Step, step.

12:16.632 --> 12:18.432
Step, step. Drag.

12:18.534 --> 12:19.771
Step, step.

12:20.833 --> 12:22.070
And under.

12:24.144 --> 12:25.702
And arm up.

12:25.804 --> 12:26.976
Good.

12:31.051 --> 12:32.014
Playing.

12:35.453 --> 12:38.917
Ready and left arm.

12:39.019 --> 12:42.357
Down, up, up. Down, up, up.

12:42.459 --> 12:43.624
And switch.

12:43.726 --> 12:45.263
(CHARLIE GRUNTS SOFTLY)

12:45.365 --> 12:46.358
(CHARLIE GROANS SOFTLY)

12:48.562 --> 12:49.928
Oh.

12:50.030 --> 12:51.631
-EMMA: Oh?
-(BOTH CHUCKLE)

12:51.733 --> 12:53.363
INSTRUCTOR: Good.

12:53.465 --> 12:56.841
And this time, Emma,
go around a full circle.

12:58.574 --> 13:00.174
(LAUGHING)

13:01.974 --> 13:03.247
INSTRUCTOR: Great.

13:03.349 --> 13:05.817
Ready and step.

13:06.713 --> 13:07.951
And turn.

13:08.517 --> 13:09.513
And step.

13:10.288 --> 13:11.616
And turn.

13:11.718 --> 13:13.088
And step.

13:14.693 --> 13:19.061
Ready and drag,
step, step, in.

13:19.726 --> 13:21.030
Turn out.

13:22.333 --> 13:23.329
Good.

13:33.178 --> 13:34.005
Oh.

13:34.108 --> 13:36.009
-(BOTH LAUGH)
-Nearly there.

13:36.111 --> 13:37.642
INSTRUCTOR: Okay, not bad.
EMMA: Okay.

13:37.744 --> 13:39.443
Not bad.

13:39.545 --> 13:41.550
Still a little difficulty
in the middle section,

13:41.652 --> 13:42.981
but overall much better.

13:43.083 --> 13:44.355
EMMA: Yeah.
CHARLIE: Thanks.

13:44.457 --> 13:45.721
Let's just do it again?

13:45.823 --> 13:47.254
-Okay.
-EMMA: (WHISPERING) Okay.

13:47.820 --> 13:48.992
What?

13:50.727 --> 13:51.962
I just... I don't know,

13:52.064 --> 13:53.363
I feel like we should
just dance normally, right?

13:53.465 --> 13:54.497
What do you mean?

13:54.599 --> 13:56.395
Well, just the... (SIGHS)

13:56.497 --> 13:59.264
I don't know, it kinda
feels a little performative.

13:59.367 --> 14:01.870
It's a wedding.
It's performative by nature.

14:01.972 --> 14:03.674
Yeah. I think
if we just do it...

14:03.776 --> 14:05.070
(SMACKS LIPS)
...a couple more times,

14:05.172 --> 14:06.572
I'm gonna get it perfect,
I swear.

14:06.674 --> 14:08.674
INSTRUCTOR: I can't make up new
choreography right on the spot.

14:08.776 --> 14:10.008
CHARLIE: Yeah.

14:10.110 --> 14:12.544
